                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Screen and diligence`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `You have PolnaChem’s financials, an ESG dossier and a stakeholder map. The target is attractive on paper, but the board now <strong>mandates two diligence lenses</strong>. The <em>ESG</em> lens: carbon intensity is <strong>+40%</strong> versus Hexagone and two sites lack EU-aligned permits — remediation is estimated at <strong>€45M</strong>. The <em>trust</em> lens: PolnaChem is <strong>founder-owned</strong>, the founder holds the top customer relationships, and a low-trust integration destroys <em>20–30% of synergy</em>. Decide how to run diligence against the rival’s clock, and what the findings really mean — what the financials alone do not show.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Price the bid`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Build the valuation. The owners want <strong>8.5x EBITDA (≈ €510M)</strong>; comparable European coatings deals trade at <strong>6.5–7.0x</strong>. Adjust the price explicitly for ESG (the <strong>€45M</strong> remediation, transition risk, the green cost-of-capital effect) and for trust (a synergy haircut for founder/customer dependency). Then set a disciplined <em>walk-away</em> and an <em>opening bid</em>: a premium over comps is only justified by synergy you can realise — and crossing your own walk-away is the winner’s curse. Every 0.1x ≈ €6M.`,
