                    insight_approved:       `Deal approved: you ran the full mandate. ESG and trust were diligenced and priced as cash flows, the bid cleared comps on realisable synergy and stayed at or below a disciplined walk-away, the structure stayed under the 2.5x ceiling with a founder lock-in, an earn-out and a sustainability-linked facility — and you held the line when the rival escalated. You won the asset and created value.`,
                    insight_walked:         `Platform lost: you walked away from a value-creating target over a priceable ESG or trust gap. The board mandated CEE entry via acquisition; over-reading a structurable exposure forfeited the platform. ESG and trust are valuation inputs to price and structure, not automatic dealbreakers.`,
                    insight_blind:          `Fast and blind: you skipped the mandated ESG and trust diligence to beat the rival — the exact failure mode that sank the last cross-border deal. Speed without diligence isn’t discipline; it’s the post-close surprise waiting to happen, and the reps you never negotiated can’t cover what you never asked.`,
                    insight_curse:          `Winner’s curse: you crossed your own walk-away to win the asset. The premium over the 6.5–7.0x comps wasn’t backed by synergy, so winning the deal destroyed acquirer value. The discipline you needed wasn’t a higher bid — it was the price you refused to pay.`,
                    insight_breach:         `Discipline breached: your structure put post-close leverage through the board’s 2.5x ceiling. The equity component you avoided and the sustainability-linked facility you skipped would have kept you under it. A deal that wins the asset but breaks the financing discipline does not clear the IC.`,
                    insight_mispriced:      `Mispriced: the ESG remediation or the trust/founder synergy haircut was left out of the bid, so the value you presented isn’t the value you can realise. The €45M and the customer dependency surface post-close — exactly the surprises this deal was designed to price in.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed outcome: parts of the case landed, but the diligence, pricing, structure and discipline didn’t fully reinforce each other. Enough gaps remain for the IC to defer — and for the two classic failure modes to find a way back in.`,
                    insight_esg:            `The single largest unpriced exposure was ESG: the €45M remediation and the transition risk never made it into the bid, so your group carbon intensity and a compliance order become a post-close shock rather than a number you negotiated down up front.`,
                    insight_trust:          `Founder/customer dependency went unmanaged: with no synergy haircut and no lock-in, the relationships the deal depended on can walk out with the founder — converting 20–30% of expected synergy into a value leak the IC was warned about.`,
                    insight_leverage:       `Post-close leverage breached the 2.5x ceiling: funding the deal all-cash without the equity or sustainability-linked structure put the group through its covenant — a discipline failure, not a financing detail.`,
                    insight_slf:            `The sustainability-linked facility worked for you: a ≈35 bps margin ratchet tied to decarbonization lowered financing cost, aligned the founder’s incentives with the net-zero pathway, and helped keep leverage under the ceiling — sustainable finance as a structuring lever.`,
                    insight_lockin:         `The founder lock-in protected the synergy: by keeping the founder and the customer relationships in, and covering the permit gap with enhanced reps, you turned the trust exposure into a structured, priced, protected position instead of a post-close leak.`,

                    hint_walked:            `You’ve walked from a priceable platform. ESG and trust gaps are valuation inputs to structure around, not automatic dealbreakers — the board mandated this entry.`,
                    hint_blind:             `You skipped the mandated diligence — the last deal’s exact failure. Without ESG and trust findings, your reps and earn-out can’t cover the surprises waiting post-close.`,
